about_footer_{year}	DNS Inspector is free & libre open source software licensed under the GNU GPLv3. DNS Inspector is copyright © 2023-{0} Ian Spence. DNS Inspector is made entirely without the use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) or Large Language Models (LLMs).
dns_server_doh_bootstrap	You can specify the IP addresses of this DNS over HTTPS server for enhanced privacy.
dns_server_target_help_dns	We connect to the DNS server using an IP address. IPv4 and IPv6 addresses are supported. To specify a port with an IPv6 address, wrap the address in square brackets. You can specify multiple IP addresses and DNS Inspector will attempt to use all of them.
dns_server_target_help_url	We connect to the DNS server using a URL. Do not include the dns query parameter.
dnssec_footer	When DNSSEC is enabled all DNS queries include a request for record signatures. DNSSEC verification will perform additional queries to establish trust and may take multiple seconds to complete.
http2_bootstrap_ip_footer	DNS Inspector does not support HTTP/2 when one or more server IP address is defined.
record_description_a	DNS A records contain an IPv4 address.
record_description_aaaa	DNS AAAA records contain an IPv6 address.
record_description_apl	DNS APL records contain an IP address prefix list.
record_description_cname	DNS CNAME records contain destination DNS name to follow.
record_description_dnskey	DNS DNSKEY records contain cryptographic public keys used for authentication.
record_description_ds	DNS DS records contain records of trusted delegation from the parent zone.
record_description_https	DNS HTTPS records contain information about HTTPS web servers.
record_description_loc	DNS LOC records contain a geographical location.
record_description_mx	DNS MX records contain mail exchange server addresses.
record_description_ns	DNS NS records contain the authoritative DNS server for this zone.
record_description_nsec	DNS NSEC records contain security information about available records in a zone.
record_description_nsec3	DNS NSEC3 contains security information about available records in a zone.
record_description_ptr	DNS PTR records are used to resolve a domain name from an IP address.
record_description_soa	DNS SOA records contain administrative or ownership information about the domain.
record_description_srv	DNS SRV records contain information for locating a specific service.
record_description_txt	DNS TXT records contain any text data.
